\title{An order whose execution's pieces each become a whole plan with the same extra presets and slot values}
\description{
The \code{using} join of a plan: an order split into the pieces its execution would send, each piece run as a whole plan of its own.

The \code{order} must be an \code{OrderPart} with exactly one execution whose pieces are known in advance, \code{ladder}, \code{twap} or \code{front_loaded}, and a timed execution must give \code{over_minutes} rather than \code{until}. UBI makes one copy of the order per piece, writes \code{each_piece}'s presets and slot values onto it, and gives each copy its piece's share: a ladder's copies their rung's price, and a timed execution's copies their slice's turn. So \code{each_piece} naming the \code{bracket} preset gives every rung of a ladder its own bracket. \code{each_piece} takes no execution, a slot given in both is refused, though presets are joined, a \code{quantity} in \code{each_piece} is refused with the rule \code{using_piece_quantity} because it would be split rather than given to each piece, a preset naming a type kept whole, such as a \code{grid}, is refused with the rule \code{using_piece_kept_whole} because it would ignore its piece's turn and price, and with a ladder neither side takes a pricing. A using join is never resized, so it cannot be a \code{then} join's child.
}
